        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You take damage from a creature or effect you can perceive.</p><hr /><p>You redistribute the harm. Reduce the damage you take by <strong>twice your level</strong>, then choose one enemy within 60 feet: it takes @Damage[2d6[spirit]] damage, and until the end of its next turn it takes a <strong>&minus;1 status penalty to saving throws</strong>.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+2)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p><p><strong>Refined (9th)</strong> The status penalty applies to <strong>AC and saving throws</strong>, and if the triggering damage would have reduced you to 0 Hit Points, you instead remain at 1 Hit Point. That last clause functions <strong>once per day</strong>.</p><hr /><p><em>Canon: damage he takes is negated, and the one who dealt it suffers for having landed it.</em></p>"
        },
